            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Anaxagoras</strong><br>\nAnaxagoras was born around 500 BCE in Clazomenae, in what is now Turkey. He was well-educated and came from a wealthy family, which allowed him to pursue his interests in philosophy. In his early years, he was influenced by the teachings of other philosophers and was particularly interested in the natural phenomena around him.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Move to Athens</strong><br>\nIn his pursuit of knowledge, Anaxagoras moved to Athens, which was the heart of intellectual activity in Greece. This city was full of thinkers, artists, and writers. It was in Athens that Anaxagoras gained a reputation for his innovative thinking and became a teacher and philosopher.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Philosophical Ideas</strong><br>\nAnaxagoras introduced the concept that everything is made up of infinitely small particles, which he called \"seeds\" or \"nous.\" He suggested that the universe was ordered by a form of intelligence or a cosmic mind, which brought order to chaos. This idea was revolutionary and laid the groundwork for many future scientific and philosophical theories.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
